33
00:02:01.075 --> 00:02:02.320
that is less prone

34
00:02:02.320 --> 00:02:07.240
to numerical rounding errors

35
00:02:07.240 --> 00:02:09.475
or really numerical under-floor.

36
00:02:09.475 --> 00:02:11.860
Because the logarithmic
function is

37
00:02:11.860 --> 00:02:16.150
a strictly monotonically
increasing function,

38
00:02:16.150 --> 00:02:18.490
we know that maximizing

39
00:02:18.490 --> 00:02:22.570
log p of y given x should
give you the same result as

40
00:02:22.570 --> 00:02:25.210
maximizing p of y given

41
00:02:25.210 --> 00:02:29.740
x as in the same value
of y that maximizes,

42
00:02:29.740 --> 00:02:32.555
this should also maximize that.

43
00:02:32.555 --> 00:02:36.700
In most implementations,
you keep track of the sum

44
00:02:36.700 --> 00:02:38.260
of logs of the probabilities

45
00:02:38.260 --> 00:02:40.945
rather than the product
of probabilities.

46
00:02:40.945 --> 00:02:44.290
Now there's one other change to

47
00:02:44.290 --> 00:02:47.110
this objective
function that makes

48
00:02:47.110 --> 00:02:51.860
the machine translation
