56
00:03:11.810 --> 00:03:13.430
If you multiply
log of the numbers

57
00:03:13.430 --> 00:03:14.510
less than one together,

58
00:03:14.510 --> 00:03:19.020
you just tend to end up
with a smaller probability.

59
00:03:19.640 --> 00:03:22.780
This objective function has

60
00:03:22.780 --> 00:03:24.610
an undesirable effect that

61
00:03:24.610 --> 00:03:27.370
it may be unnaturally
tend to prefer

62
00:03:27.370 --> 00:03:30.070
very short
translations to prefer

63
00:03:30.070 --> 00:03:33.590
very short outputs because

64
00:03:33.590 --> 00:03:35.790
the probability of
a short sentence is

65
00:03:35.790 --> 00:03:39.110
just by multiplying fewer
of these numbers are

66
00:03:39.110 --> 00:03:42.390
less than one and

67
00:03:42.390 --> 00:03:46.250
so the product will just
be not quite as small.

68
00:03:46.250 --> 00:03:48.980
By the way, the same
thing is true for this,

69
00:03:48.980 --> 00:03:50.870
the log of a probability is

70
00:03:50.870 --> 00:03:54.945
always less than
or equal to one,

71
00:03:54.945 --> 00:03:56.960
you're actually in
this range of the log,

72
00:03:56.960 --> 00:03:59.000
so the more terms
you add together,

73
00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:02.610
the more negative
this thing becomes.

74
00:04:04.070 --> 00:04:06.700
There's one other
change the algorithm

75
