lot of different options,

145
00:07:27.640 --> 00:07:29.950
but it will be slower.

146
00:07:29.950 --> 00:07:32.140
The memory requirements
will also grow and

147
00:07:32.140 --> 00:07:35.065
also be computationally slower.

148
00:07:35.065 --> 00:07:37.660
Whereas if you use a
very small beam width,

149
00:07:37.660 --> 00:07:40.960
then you get a worse result
because you are just keeping

150
00:07:40.960 --> 00:07:45.470
less possibilities in mind
as the algorithm is running,

151
00:07:45.470 --> 00:07:48.010
but you get a result faster and

152
00:07:48.010 --> 00:07:50.800
the memory requirements
will also be lower.

153
00:07:50.800 --> 00:07:53.050
In the previous video,

154
00:07:53.050 --> 00:07:56.520
we use in our running
